Subj: U/L the CNet demo EVERYWHERE 
From: Bill Beogelein  (SysOp)
Orgz: CNet-BBS V3.05a Beta-Tester
On  : Mon  7-Feb-1994  5:20p

I think more non-CNet SysOps are checking out the CNet-demo than we realize.

Everyone can help.  Make it file-fequ'able on your system.

I use MagicNames "CNetDemo1" and "CNetDemo2".
> CNetDemo1 609K CNet-BBS v3.04 freely distributable demo. Disk #1 of 2. Jan94
> CNetDemo2 348K CNet-BBS v3.04 freely distributable demo. Disk #2 of 2. Jan94

If we all use the same MagicNames, more people will be able to find it.  It
would be great if we could someday say, "Just file-requ CNetDemo1 and
CNetDemo2 from any one of ~1000 CNet-BBSs anywhere in the world."  And get the
latest demo.

Also, U/L it everywhere.  Add it into disk collections, CD-ROMs, FTP-sites,
etc.

Make it a "Free" D/L on your system.  Make it available to first-time callers.
Add it to the "QuickDL.LHA" pfile list.  With QuickDL.lha you can add a "DEMO"
cmd to any menu that D/Ls the demo.  We could tell everyone in the world,
"Just call any CNet and type 'DEMO' at any prompt".

Post msgs in echos that a CNet-demo is *now* available.  Add it to your
news-files.  Log-in/log-out screens.  Mention it in your Fidonet, Usenet, and
local msg signature-lines.  Mention it in all your "zzzBBSad" archive files.

How many of the 10,000,000 users in the Internet know about it?

-Bill Allen Beogelein, CNet Beta-Tester v3.05a-Beta, 1:2410/207, 1-810-473-2020

